  "cleanText": "Solution home \n\t\tCapium 365\n\t\tCapium 365 (Accountant)\n\n### CAPIUM 365: Recording CIS\n\n\t\t\tPrint\n\n\tModified on: Mon, 21 Jul, 2025 at  3:43 PM\n\n\t\tThis guide explains how to apply and remove CIS (Construction Industry Scheme) deductions within the Books section of Capium 365.\n\nNote: Books section is only available for individuals and sole traders who are not registered for VAT. For customers above the VAT threshold or other entities (i.e. Limited Companies and Partnerships) the software will post the invoices and purchases directly to the Bookkeeping module.\n\nNavigation: Capium 365 > Books\n\n### \n\n### Adding a CIS Deduction\n\nUse this option to apply a CIS deduction percentage to a transaction you’ve already added to your Books section.\n\n### Steps:\n\nGo to Capium 365 > Books.\n\nFind the relevant transaction by scrolling, filtering, or using the search bar.\n\nHover over the transaction.\n\nClick the ‘+’ icon on the right-hand side.\n\nEnter the CIS deduction percentage.\n\nClick Save.\n\nSee screenshots below for reference:\n\nRemoving a CIS Deduction\n\nIf you’ve applied a CIS deduction by mistake or need to remove it, follow these steps.\n\n### Steps:\n\nGo to Capium 365 > Books.\n\nFind the transaction using scroll, filter, or search.\n\nHover over the transaction.\n\nClick the three dots (⋮) on the right-hand side.\n\nSelect Delete to remove the CIS deduction.\n\nSee screenshot below for reference:\n\n### Adding a Transaction\n\nBefore applying CIS deductions, ensure your transactions are added to the Books section. Transactions can be added manually, via upload, or through a bank feed.\n\nClick here to learn how to add and manage transactions in Capium 365\n\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tDid you find it helpful?\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tYes\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\tNo\n\nSend feedback\tSorry we couldn't be helpful. Help us improve this article with your feedback.",
